    "wordCount": 99,
    "readMinutes": 1,
    "searchText": "ADR 0001: Enforce layered dependency direction Status: Accepted Date: 2026-07-21 Context The provider spans byte transport, PostgreSQL protocol semantics, ADO.NET, replication, EF Core, and optional extensions. Mixing these concerns would make wire behaviour hard to test and force low-level packages to inherit volatile dependencies. Decision Use the dependency direction in `docs/architecture/overview.md`. Protocol code cannot expose ADO.NET concepts; Data cannot expose EF Core concepts. Optional extensions integrate through `BlueTusk.Extensions.Abstractions`. Consequences Some operations require orchestration types in `BlueTusk.Client` even when most of their implementation is lower-level. Cross-layer convenience APIs belong in the highest applicable layer.",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "html",
        "html": "<h1>ADR 0001: Enforce layered dependency direction</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Status: Accepted</li>\n<li>Date: 2026-07-21</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Context</h2>\n<p>The provider spans byte transport, PostgreSQL protocol semantics, ADO.NET, replication, EF Core, and optional extensions. Mixing these concerns would make wire behaviour hard to test and force low-level packages to inherit volatile dependencies.</p>\n<h2>Decision</h2>\n<p>Use the dependency direction in <code>docs/architecture/overview.md</code>. Protocol code cannot expose ADO.NET concepts; Data cannot expose EF Core concepts. Optional extensions integrate through <code>BlueTusk.Extensions.Abstractions</code>.</p>\n<h2>Consequences</h2>\n<p>Some operations require orchestration types in <code>BlueTusk.Client</code> even when most of their implementation is lower-level. Cross-layer convenience APIs belong in the highest applicable layer.</p>\n"
      }
    ]
